==============================================================================
Part 4: referee's OWN from-scratch Beta-integral derivation (own
algebra, independent of the target's docstring), fully checked
==============================================================================
Step 0 (Beta integral): int_0^1 x^(t+r)(1-x)^K dx = (t+r)! K! / (K+t+r+1)!
  standard Beta(a+1,b+1)=a!b!/(a+b+1)! identity, a=t+r, b=K.
  Beta-integral identity checked at 64 deterministic (a,b) integer pairs (0<=a,b<=7): ALL OK

Combining Part 1 (P_K(x,t) closed form, symbolic K,t) with Step 0 gives
  K! S(K,t) = int_0^1 x^t (1-x)^K P_K(x,t) dx
            = int_0^1 x^t (1-x)^K (1+x)^(K-1) [(t+1)(1+x)+2Kx] dx
Using (1-x)^K(1+x)^(K-1) = (1-x)(1-x^2)^(K-1) (elementary, checked below,
symbolic K):
  (1-x)^K(1+x)^(K-1) - (1-x)(1-x^2)^(K-1), symbolic integer K, simplified: (1 - x)**Ki*(x + 1)**(Ki - 1) + (1 - x**2)**(Ki - 1)*(x - 1)

  x^t(1-x)^K P_K(x,t) = x^t(1-x^2)^(K-1)(1-x)[(t+1)(1+x)+2Kx]
     = x^t(1-x^2)^(K-1)[(t+1)(1-x^2) + 2Kx(1-x)]     [multiply out (1-x)(...)]
     = (t+1) x^t(1-x^2)^K + 2K x^(t+1)(1-x^2)^(K-1) - 2K x^(t+2)(1-x^2)^(K-1)
  Integrating term by term over [0,1] and recognizing
  f_K(x):=2K x(1-x^2)^(K-1) (the ALREADY-PROVED M_K density, Estagio 24):
    K! S(K,t) = (t+1) int x^t(1-x^2)^K dx  +  mu_t  -  mu_{t+1}
  where mu_s := int_0^1 x^s f_K(x) dx = E[M_K^s].
  By Part 2's IBP identity: (t+1) int x^t(1-x^2)^K dx = mu_{t+1} EXACTLY.
  Substituting: K! S(K,t) = mu_{t+1} + mu_t - mu_{t+1} = mu_t.
  Hence S(K,t) = mu_t / K! = Gamma(t/2+1)/Gamma(K+t/2+1)  [standard Beta-
  integral evaluation of mu_t, checked independently below, symbolic t,
  K=1..25 in Part 3, and via fresh symbolic integration for K=1..10 here]:

